Subject: [PATCH] display: REIMS_VGPU_DISPLAY_SIZE, a mode in the host screen's shape

A phone's screen is nearer 19.5:9 than 16:9, and a 16:9 desktop sits between
black bars on it. REIMS_VGPU_DISPLAY_SIZE=WIDTHxHEIGHT (even sides, 640x360
to 1920x1080 pixels) makes that the guest's only mode, and the panel the guest
is told about takes the same shape: the height stays 27 cm and the width is
the whole centimetre that keeps the pixels square. It takes precedence over
REIMS_VGPU_DISPLAY_MODE; out of bounds or unparseable, it is refused on the
failure channel and the other modes are offered.

reims-vgpu-config gains dimensions(), which parses WIDTHxHEIGHT and hands back
what it cannot, as choice() does.

